<!--
  MANYWATERS_COLOR_SUPPORT_1 v1 — added scope, owner verbatim (paraphrased from
  voice, 2026-09-09): "if the thirst kid is present, we should have different
  bottles of the colored waters too. Conditional mod check."

  IDENTIFIED, live modlist (not guessed): the mod is **Dubs Bad Hygiene**, split
  into `Dubwise.DubsBadHygiene.Lite` (packageId confirmed at
  `.../workshop/content/294100/2570319432/About/About.xml`) + the
  `Dubwise.DubsBadHygiene.Thirst` add-on (packageId confirmed at
  `.../2582878800/About/About.xml`, description "Adds a thirst need to Dubs Bad
  Hygiene Lite") — both active in ModsConfig.xml. The drinkable item itself,
  `DBH_WaterBottle`, is defined IN Lite's own `1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/
  Items_Resource_Stuff.xml:108-167` (ParentName="ResourceBasedMom",
  `modExtensions/WaterExt` with `SeekForThirst=true`) — Thirst has no Defs of its
  own, it only supplies the `Need_Thirst` class Lite's own NeedDef references. So
  the correct gate for a `DBH_WaterBottle` clone is Lite's packageId: if Lite is
  inactive, `DBH_WaterBottle` itself does not exist and `ParentName` would dangle.

  Each variant below only overrides defName/label/description/colour; everything
  else (the `WaterExt` modExtension, `ingestible` block, stack/mass stats) is
  inherited from `DBH_WaterBottle` unchanged, so these drink and satisfy thirst
  exactly like the vanilla bottle — same texture (`DBH/Things/Resource/
  WaterBottles`), tinted via `graphicData.color` the same way the terrain and fleck
  variants are, per this item's colour set (Defs/TerrainDefs/RM_ColoredWater.xml).

  `MayRequire` on the TerrainDef tag itself (not a PatchOperationFindMod file) —
  the whole node is skipped, never loaded, never a dangling ParentName error, when
  Lite is absent. Never ungated, per the owner's own instruction.

  🔴 FIXED 2026-09-10 (DIRTY_CODE_REVIEW_STANDING_LOOP_1, live NRE lead from
  Player_log_manywaters_thingclass_NRE_2026-09-09.log — five "Config error in
  RM_WaterBottle_*: has null thingClass" lines, one per variant): the original
  `ParentName="DBH_WaterBottle"` never resolved. Verified against the live donor
  XML (Items_Resource_Stuff.xml:108-109 in Dubs Bad Hygiene Lite): DBH_WaterBottle
  is declared `<ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBasedMom" DBHThirst="true">` with only
  a `<defName>` element — it has no `Name="..."` XML attribute. RimWorld's
  XmlInheritance resolves ParentName only against another def's `Name=` attribute
  (registered in nodesByName), never against defName as a fallback — the same
  engine-verified trap already documented in
  `src/RimStarWars/UtinniPatches/Defs/BiomeDefs/RUT_NightsideIce.xml`. So every
  field below was silently uninherited: null thingClass (hence the config error),
  no WaterExt modExtension (no thirst-seeking behaviour at all), no ingestible
  block, no stats. Fixed by inheriting from `ResourceBasedMom` instead (it DOES
  carry `Name="ResourceBasedMom"`, so that link is real) and restating
  DBH_WaterBottle's own delta on top of it — statBases/comps/thingCategories are
  list fields that APPEND under XmlInheritance, so this reproduces exactly what
  `ParentName="DBH_WaterBottle"` would have produced had it worked.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef MayRequire="Dubwise.DubsBadHygiene.Lite" ParentName="ResourceBasedMom">
    <defName>RM_WaterBottle_Rust</defName>
    <label>rust-tinted water</label>
    <description>A bottle of water carrying enough dissolved iron oxide to run the colour of old blood. Still drinkable — just don't ask where it came from.</description>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="DubsBadHygiene.WaterExt">
        <water>1</water>
        <UseForWashing>true</UseForWashing>
        <SeekForThirst>true</SeekForThirst>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>DBH/Things/Resource/WaterBottles</texPath>
      <graphicClass>DubsBadHygiene.Graphic_StackCountTech</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>0.8</drawSize>
      <color>(168,92,58)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties">
        <compClass>DubsBadHygiene.CompContamination</compClass>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>60</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.2</Flammability>
      <Mass>0.5</Mass>
    </statBases>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>Foods</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <generateAllowChance>0</generateAllowChance>
    <generateCommonality>0</generateCommonality>
    <stackLimit>10</stackLimit>
    <tradeNeverStack>false</tradeNeverStack>
    <tradeability>None</tradeability>
    <ingestible>
      <baseIngestTicks>240</baseIngestTicks>
      <preferability>NeverForNutrition</preferability>
      <foodType>Fluid</foodType>
      <nurseable>false</nurseable>
      <ingestSound>Ingest_Beer</ingestSound>
      <ingestHoldOffsetStanding>
        <northDefault>
          <offset>(0.18,0,0)</offset>
        </northDefault>
      </ingestHoldOffsetStanding>
      <ingestCommandString>Drink {0}</ingestCommandString>
      <ingestReportString>Drinking {0}.</ingestReportString>
      <chairSearchRadius>5</chairSearchRadius>
    </ingestible>
  </ThingDef>

